# Load-limited gripper close BY ITSELF (no planner, executor or arm motion): close slowly until the gripper's motor load
# reaches close/load_target, hold there, and report. Blocks until finished (call it from a client with no short timeout).
# execute:=false only watches the load and sends nothing to the gripper. Refused (success=false, nothing sent) when the
# e-stop is engaged or unknown, or when there is no joint_6 measurement or no fresh /arm_interface/motor_load.
bool execute             # false: watch only, the gripper is not commanded
bool open_first          # ramp to gripper_open first (at gripper_speed), then close
---
bool success             # the close finished (outcome set); false: refused, faulted or timed out (see message)
string outcome           # 'object' (load target reached and held) | 'thin' (closed completely below it) | 'not executed' | ''
string message
float64 load_percent     # gripper |load| in % of max torque at the end
